    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with an elite efficiency score of 81.87. He benefits from a confluence of positive indicators against Bello, specifically a significant platoon advantage and a favorable wind forecast that boosts his slugging potential. Furthermore, his BvP history is stellar, and his slotting in the #2 hole ensures maximum plate appearance volume. **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** also project as high-upside options; while both await official confirmation of their lineup slots, their ability to capitalize on the moderate skill profile of Nelson provides a solid floor for our outfield production.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility spot and final infield positions remains heavily dictated by our 40.0 efficiency threshold. **Jackson Merrill** holds a marginal score of 51.97, surviving the cut largely due to a platoon advantage, though he faces a difficult matchup against the elite Wheeler. Consequently, **Miguel Andujar** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his score of 34.66 fell well below our floor requirement. Despite a decent base projection, his negative platoon split against the right-handed Wheeler and a lower-leverage batting position pushed him to the bench to preserve our game caps.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** closely, as his matchup against the elite Chris Sale is our most significant volatility risk. While his score of 55.25 remains acceptable, his efficiency is hampered by Sale\u2019s high skill level, requiring us to hedge our expectations for power production. We continue to navigate the roster with caution regarding health, as **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on our healthy starters to maintain our standing in the scarce stolen base category.",
